{
  "sheet": "skills",
  "about": "One row per skill (5 per hero). slot: primary=M1 gun, secondary=M2 (Deadlock ability 1), utility=Shift (ability 2), special=R (ability 3), ult=F (Deadlock ultimate, locked until its charge meter fills). Numbers are RoR2-scale: damagePct is % of the body's damage stat (RoR2 convention), cooldowns are RoR2 seconds. deadlock* columns hold the source values read from the player's Deadlock scripts/abilities.vdata (ClientVersion 6774) so every conversion is traceable. kind picks the generic EntityState that implements the row. Unused numeric params are 0, unused refs are \"none\" (filled on purpose, not missing). Balance targets: sustained primary DPS 300-450 %/s (Commando Double Tap ~ 400 %/s incl. downtime); secondaries 2-8 s; utilities 4-10 s; specials 8-14 s; ultimates 1500-3000 % total, gated by ultCharge. castAmount: what a buff ability also does the moment it is cast (haze_fixation: Fixation stacks put on enemies in the crosshair cone within range/spreadDeg; abrams_resilience: fraction of max health healed over the duration; seven_power_surge: % damage of the zap that hits every enemy within radius on cast; 0 = nothing extra). expect: what the skill must measurably do, checked in test mode (enemy_damage, enemy_stun, enemy_burn, enemy_debuff:<buff>, self_buff:<buff>, self_heal, self_move, self_cloak).",
